{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["And He added in the exposition of the commandment Honor, <b>as YHWH your Elohim commanded you</b> — from the mouth of the Gevurah, as I explained (Ramban on Deuteronomy 5:12), and therefore He added, 'so that it may go well with you,' as it is said (Psalms 85:13), 'YHWH will also grant what is good, and our land will yield its produce.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Reading הַגְּבוּרָה ('the Gevurah') as a divine epithet; Ramban uses it to refer to the divine source of the commandment at Sinai/Horeb, consistent with his argument in the comment on Deuteronomy 5:12."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:36.666636015Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}